  <lyrics>
    <verse name="v1">
      <lines>
      <chord name="F7"/>My heart can <chord name="Bb"/>sing when I pause to re<chord name="F7"/>member,<br/>
      A heartache <chord name="F"/>here is but a stepping <chord name="Bb"/>stone.<br/>
      <chord name="F7"/>Along a <chord name="Bb"/>trail, that&#x27;s winding <chord name="F7"/>al<chord name="Bb"/>ways <chord name="Eb"/>upward,<br/>
      This troubled <chord name="Bb"/>world, is not my <chord name="C7"/>final <chord name="Bb"/>home.<br/>
      But until <chord name="Cm"/>then, my <chord name="F7"/>heart will go on <chord name="Bb"/>singing,<chord name="F7"/><chord name="Bb"/><br/>
      Until <chord name="Cm"/>then, with <chord name="F7"/>joy I&#x27;ll carry <chord name="Bb"/>on,<br/>
      Un<chord name="F7"/>til the <chord name="Bb"/>day <chord name="F7"/>my <chord name="G7"/>eyes behold the <chord name="Cm"/>city,<chord name="A7"/><br/>
      Until the <chord name="Bb"/>day God calls <chord name="F7"/>me <chord name="Bb"/>home.
      </lines>
    </verse>
    <verse name="c1">
      <lines>
      <chord name="F7"/>But until then, <chord name="Bb"/>my heart will <chord name="F7"/>go on singing,<br/>
      <chord name="F"/>Until then, with <chord name="Bb"/>joy I&#x27;ll carry on,<br/>
      <chord name="F7"/>Until <chord name="Bb"/>the day <chord name="F7"/>my <chord name="Bb"/>eyes behold <chord name="Eb"/>the city,<br/>
      <chord name="Bb"/>Until the <chord name="C7"/>day God <chord name="Bb"/>calls me home.
      </lines>
    </verse>
    <verse name="v2">
      <lines>
      <chord name="F7"/>The things of <chord name="Bb"/>earth will dim <chord name="F7"/>and loose there value,<br/>
      <chord name="F"/>If we recall <chord name="Bb"/>they&#x27;re borrowed for awhile;<br/>
      <chord name="F7"/>And things <chord name="Bb"/>of earth <chord name="F7"/>that cause <chord name="Bb"/>the heart <chord name="Eb"/>to tremble,<br/>
      <chord name="Bb"/>Remember there, <chord name="C7"/>will only <chord name="Bb"/>bring a smile.
      </lines>
    </verse>
